{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790349524,"nonce":"8nbV5+dax+TMSVfxM90SJbT7mQ0=","title":"zynml run prints about 390 \"declared in this program and again\" warnings for any program that imports the prelude","message":"`zynml run crates/zynml/examples/test_02_println_int.zynml` prints its three lines on stdout and 392 warnings on stderr, every one of the form \"'$Tensor$sum_f32' is declared in this program and again in this program; calls to it reach the last one declared\" or \"'concat' is declared in this program and again in prelude\". The count is the same under --profile classic and tiered-dev. The warning is collect_declarations' (crates/compiler/src/lowering.rs:2210, from 80a1bc8), and zynml's default log filter is warn, so every run shows it. The duplicates are the grammar's @builtin externs, the prelude's own `extern def`s and the imported modules declaring the same runtime symbols, which is by design, so either those declarations are merged before collection or the warning is kept for two bodies under one name. NUC x86_64, main 19697230.","files":null}]}